index 0000000000..801af115d2
--- /dev/null
+++ b/projects/ROCKNIX/packages/network/raofflineproxy/patches/005-keep-the-refresh-thread-alive.patch
@@ -0,0 +1,182 @@
+proxy_service: keep the refresh thread alive through a failed pass
+
+PeriodicRefresh has no exception boundary: refresh_game_patch raises
+CacheGameError on any network or API failure, and one such raised out of
+run(), ended the daemon thread, and the service ran on with no refresh
+and no eviction until its next start -- Restart=on-failure never sees a
+dead thread (ROCKNIX audit #186 PL-25). A pass now catches per game: a
+refused sign-in (CacheGameAuthError) ends the pass without a request for
+every remaining game, three failures in a row end it, anything else is
+logged and the next game is tried; and run() catches around the whole
+pass, so the next pass runs an hour later whatever happened in this one.
+
+This patch used to bound the pass as well -- the oldest patch rows first,
+50 a pass, a 24 h floor -- because the fork lifts the 100-game cap (patch
+004) and the client then refreshed every cached game every hour. Upstream
+59b167c scopes the pass to the games played in the last seven days, which
+bounds it by what the player plays rather than by the size of the library,
+so that half was retired when the fork moved to 0711f0b (fork
+maxengel/rocknix#259, ROCKNIX D-RA-029).
+
+Written for ROCKNIX (fork issue maxengel/rocknix#186, PL-25). Offered
+upstream as-is (ROCKNIX D-RA-016: whatever the fork changes in the proxy
+goes back).
+
+--- a/linux/raofflineproxy/proxy_service.py
++++ b/linux/raofflineproxy/proxy_service.py
+@@ -46,6 +46,7 @@ from .network import (
